# BUGS

Only the floor tier's kernels are built: they run at about the speed of memory, and a copy for x86-64-v3 composed no faster.
A blend through partial alpha goes a pixel at a time, as light(2)'s tables are lookups the floor's vectors can't gather.
UICore's renderer still blends a shape's corners and sides and its glow there, dots, a gradient's edges across it, icons, pictures and glyphs from distance fields a pixel at a time.
